    "suggested_action": "replace_ja_expression",
    "reason": "While 監督 (kantoku) can sometimes mean 'manager' (as listed in JMdict glosses), its primary and most common uses are for 'director' (e.g., film director), 'coach' (e.g., sports coach), or 'supervisor' (e.g., construction site supervisor). It is semantically broader than the English 'manager' and not the most natural or common term a general learner would expect for a business or organizational 'manager'. The loanword マネージャー (maneejaa) is a more direct and natural fit for the general concept of 'manager' in modern Japanese.",
